From: NeoDarwin
Subject: [PATCH] libutil: tzlink without tzlinkd

tzlink(3) asks the tzlinkd daemon over XPC to repoint /etc/localtime.
NeoDarwin runs no tzlinkd yet, and its libxpc stand-in has no XPC
connections (nor xpc_dictionary_get_uint64, which only this call uses). Add a
LIBUTIL_NO_TZLINKD switch that selects the simulator's version, which
returns ENOTSUP.

Rebase-risk: low (one preprocessor condition).
---
diff --git a/tzlink.c b/tzlink.c
--- a/tzlink.c
+++ b/tzlink.c
@@ -31,7 +31,11 @@
 errno_t
 tzlink(const char *tz)
 {
-#if TARGET_OS_IPHONE || TARGET_OS_OSX && !TARGET_OS_SIMULATOR
+/*
+ * LIBUTIL_NO_TZLINKD: build without tzlinkd, with the simulator's version,
+ * which returns ENOTSUP.
+ */
+#if (TARGET_OS_IPHONE || TARGET_OS_OSX && !TARGET_OS_SIMULATOR) && !defined(LIBUTIL_NO_TZLINKD)
 	xpc_connection_t connection;
 	xpc_object_t request, reply;
 	errno_t e;
